523
00:18:27,772 --> 00:18:29,372
What's this? Is it a snow crab? No.

524
00:18:29,372 --> 00:18:30,442
- What? - It's huge.

525
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:31,512
The crab is huge.

526
00:18:32,572 --> 00:18:35,812
(A bite of blue crab as big as a snow crab)

527
00:18:35,982 --> 00:18:38,552
If this place is real, I'd love to come here again.

528
00:18:38,552 --> 00:18:39,652
What's more...

529
00:18:39,652 --> 00:18:41,752
The production crew always brings us...

530
00:18:41,752 --> 00:18:43,982
to the tastiest place first.

531
00:18:43,982 --> 00:18:45,292
(Digging in)

532
00:18:45,292 --> 00:18:46,322
Because...

533
00:18:46,992 --> 00:18:48,662
you have to hook viewers from the start.

534
00:18:49,522 --> 00:18:52,232
That's a practical take. I'd expect nothing less.

535
00:18:52,232 --> 00:18:53,232
She should know.

536
00:18:53,762 --> 00:18:56,032
You need something visually impressive right from the start.

537
00:18:56,902 --> 00:18:58,902
- That keeps viewers watching. - To keep viewers watching.

538
00:18:58,902 --> 00:19:00,002
(Good visuals bring in the ratings.)

539
00:19:00,002 --> 00:19:01,172
- You get it, right? - Yes.

540
00:19:01,172 --> 00:19:02,372
I learn a lot from you.

541
00:19:03,942 --> 00:19:06,542
(Quietly shelling the seafood)

542
00:19:07,212 --> 00:19:09,612
Guys, isn't it a hassle to eat this food?

543
00:19:10,212 --> 00:19:12,552
No matter how much I shell, I can't see the bottom.

544
00:19:13,312 --> 00:19:14,982
Shell them as you eat, like us.

545
00:19:16,052 --> 00:19:18,422
I'm the type who shells everything first and eats it all at once.

546
00:19:18,422 --> 00:19:19,692
- Same here. - You too, right?

547
00:19:19,692 --> 00:19:20,722
Yes.

548
00:19:20,722 --> 00:19:22,892
Let's shell some more once we've eaten this batch.

549
00:19:22,892 --> 00:19:25,332
(Inconvenient for those who like to do all the prep first?)

550
00:19:25,592 --> 00:19:28,102
- What's this? - That's cute.

551
00:19:28,102 --> 00:19:29,362
It's in the shape of a dinosaur.

552
00:19:29,362 --> 00:19:30,362
(Dinosaur fish cake)

553
00:19:30,362 --> 00:19:31,732
- Really? - It's a dinosaur.

554
00:19:31,732 --> 00:19:33,002
The head and the leg.

555
00:19:33,132 --> 00:19:35,642
It's cute. I think it's fish cake.

556
00:19:35,642 --> 00:19:36,742
(Cute dinosaur fish cakes that kids would love)

557
00:19:36,742 --> 00:19:37,912
Look.

558
00:19:38,142 --> 00:19:39,712
It's in the shape of a triceratops.

559
00:19:42,382 --> 00:19:43,382
(Impressed)

560
00:19:44,142 --> 00:19:45,212
It's delicious.

561
00:19:46,652 --> 00:19:48,052
Have some, Eun I.

562
00:19:48,452 --> 00:19:50,552
I'm standing up because I can't see anything.

563
00:19:50,882 --> 00:19:51,952
But you can, right?

564
00:19:52,752 --> 00:19:54,022
You can see it sitting down, can't you?

565
00:19:54,022 --> 00:19:55,022
I can't.

566
00:19:55,592 --> 00:19:57,992
I can't see what's inside the pot when I'm sitting down.

567
00:19:58,532 --> 00:20:00,832
That's why I'm standing up. Don't worry about me.

568
00:20:01,032 --> 00:20:02,562
We're forced into a standing party.

569
00:20:04,102 --> 00:20:05,432
You want to see the bottom, right?

570
00:20:05,432 --> 00:20:06,702
You want to know what's at the bottom, right?

571
00:20:06,702 --> 00:20:07,872
For real.

572
00:20:08,202 --> 00:20:09,372
(Staring)

573
00:20:09,372 --> 00:20:12,112
Your outfit and those tongs really don't go together.

574
00:20:13,442 --> 00:20:15,212
(Feeling small)

575
00:20:15,212 --> 00:20:17,042
I even wore a necklace because...

576
00:20:17,482 --> 00:20:19,582
- I was coming on this show today. - I noticed.

577
00:20:19,582 --> 00:20:22,082
- I dolled up today. - I see.

578
00:20:22,282 --> 00:20:23,522
But it was too much.

579
00:20:23,522 --> 00:20:24,622
(His confidence fades.)

580
00:20:24,992 --> 00:20:26,822
(Kid Yu is having fun teasing his younger friend again.)

581
00:20:26,822 --> 00:20:27,862
You...

582
00:20:27,862 --> 00:20:29,962
Now that we're eating, I've noticed a downside.

583
00:20:30,492 --> 00:20:31,862
Because of how the pot is designed,

584
00:20:31,862 --> 00:20:33,892
the delicious sauce gathers at the bottom.

585
00:20:33,892 --> 00:20:35,902
Right? There's not enough sauce on top.

586
00:20:36,232 --> 00:20:37,562
I agree with Eun I.

587
00:20:38,172 --> 00:20:41,202
- You've got to dip the seafood... - Like a dip.

588
00:20:41,202 --> 00:20:42,302
into the sauce and such.

589
00:20:42,442 --> 00:20:44,972
- But you've got to dig into it. - You have to search for the sauce.

590
00:20:44,972 --> 00:20:46,742
(A design that makes it hard to dip into the sauce?)

591
00:20:46,742 --> 00:20:50,412
The owner could easily buy braised seafood somewhere else...

592
00:20:50,412 --> 00:20:51,412
- and pour it in here. - Totally.

593
00:20:51,412 --> 00:20:53,382
You're right. You could just pour it...

594
00:20:53,382 --> 00:20:54,382
- into the pot. - Yes.

595
00:20:54,382 --> 00:20:55,382
(Could it be fake, with store-bought braised seafood poured in?)

596
00:20:55,382 --> 00:20:57,052
Hyun Ji has a good eye for detail.

597
00:20:57,052 --> 00:20:58,252
She's a detective.

598
00:20:58,522 --> 00:21:01,092
Another problem with this pot is that...

599
00:21:01,592 --> 00:21:02,892
When the food gets cold as you eat it,

600
00:21:02,892 --> 00:21:05,292
you need to be able to reheat it.

601
00:21:05,462 --> 00:21:07,462
- But you can't with this pot. - No.

602
00:21:07,462 --> 00:21:08,562
(You can't put it over a flame to reheat it.)

603
00:21:08,762 --> 00:21:10,132
Jae Seok, braised dishes aren't...

604
00:21:10,132 --> 00:21:11,402
You rarely reheat braised dishes.

605
00:21:11,402 --> 00:21:13,732
- Come on, some people do reheat it. - What?

606
00:21:14,872 --> 00:21:17,502
- He's in a pinch. - The braised dish is...

607
00:21:17,502 --> 00:21:18,572
- served on a plate, - Hey.

608
00:21:18,572 --> 00:21:19,642
which the owner takes away later...

609
00:21:19,642 --> 00:21:20,772
- We were... - to make fried rice.

610
00:21:20,772 --> 00:21:22,982
We were starting to think this place is fake.

611
00:21:23,542 --> 00:21:26,182
I was just trying to back up that claim.

612
00:21:27,452 --> 00:21:30,082
The container does keep the food warm for longer.

613
00:21:30,082 --> 00:21:32,022
If you think about it,

614
00:21:32,222 --> 00:21:33,352
you can throw the bigger ingredients...

615
00:21:33,352 --> 00:21:34,492
- in here. - Yes.

616
00:21:34,492 --> 00:21:36,322
- There's a reason behind it. - Of course.

617
00:21:36,322 --> 00:21:38,492
Listen. Here's what I noticed.

618
00:21:38,492 --> 00:21:40,432
See the rim?

619
00:21:40,432 --> 00:21:41,762
- Yes. - They're all different.

620
00:21:41,962 --> 00:21:44,732
There must be several of these eggs. If the rims are all different...

621
00:21:44,732 --> 00:21:45,732
How do you find the pairs after washing them?

622
00:21:45,732 --> 00:21:46,802
Exactly.

623
00:21:46,902 --> 00:21:49,702
If I were the owner, I'd just cut the rim straight.

624
00:21:50,402 --> 00:21:52,272
- It wouldn't look egg-like. - Right?

625
00:21:52,572 --> 00:21:54,072
The pattern makes it look like an egg.

626
00:21:55,712 --> 00:21:57,642
When you put it like that, I can't argue.

627
00:21:58,812 --> 00:22:00,012
This is hilarious.

628
00:22:00,012 --> 00:22:02,522
- We'd have to argue it out. - It's so funny.

629
00:22:02,522 --> 00:22:04,792
- You and I have to argue it out. - No, we don't have to.

630
00:22:04,792 --> 00:22:05,852
Today's confrontation is...

631
00:22:05,852 --> 00:22:06,922
- interesting. - It's funny.

632
00:22:06,922 --> 00:22:09,862
(The members are passionate about their opposing views today.)

633
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:11,892
I should've asked for the owner's name.

634
00:22:11,892 --> 00:22:12,892
- Why? - Why?

635
00:22:12,892 --> 00:22:14,162
It said Chef Choi.

636
00:22:14,162 --> 00:22:16,362
(The sign they saw earlier)

637
00:22:17,262 --> 00:22:19,472
- "Chef Choi's Grilled Clams." - Right.

638
00:22:19,472 --> 00:22:21,442
Only the "Chef Choi" part looks too new.

639
00:22:22,572 --> 00:22:24,512
Maybe it has to do with Chef Choi Hyun Seok.

640
00:22:24,512 --> 00:22:25,972
- Again? - Yes.

641
00:22:25,972 --> 00:22:27,112
(Did they just change to "Chef Choi?")

642
00:22:27,472 --> 00:22:29,512
What if the owner says, "Hi, I'm Kim?"

643
00:22:29,512 --> 00:22:31,552
- Yes, it's possible. - That makes sense.

644
00:22:31,982 --> 00:22:33,182
But it should be Chef Choi.

645
00:22:33,452 --> 00:22:35,182
The owner could awkwardly say,

646
00:22:35,182 --> 00:22:37,782
- "But the chef is Choi." - "The chef is Choi."

647
00:22:37,782 --> 00:22:39,822
"I'm Kim, the owner."

648
00:22:39,952 --> 00:22:41,122
Exactly.

649
00:22:41,122 --> 00:22:43,962
"I'm the son-in-law."

650
00:22:43,962 --> 00:22:46,492
Sang Yeob, don't ridicule the owner too much.

651
00:22:49,102 --> 00:22:50,402
(Feeling sheepish in his stead)

652
00:22:50,402 --> 00:22:52,432
You were making fun of him with that impression.

653
00:22:52,432 --> 00:22:53,772
(Why only me again?)

654
00:22:53,772 --> 00:22:55,472
- That's why I'm nagging at you. - I see.

655
00:22:55,802 --> 00:22:58,142
- I was just joining in. - I know.

656
00:22:58,142 --> 00:22:59,342
That was thoughtless.

657
00:22:59,542 --> 00:23:01,212
- I'm used to it. - Right.

658
00:23:01,212 --> 00:23:02,382
(This familiar feeling)

659
00:23:02,382 --> 00:23:03,582
Shall we get going now?

660
00:23:03,712 --> 00:23:04,852
- Okay. - Good.

661
00:23:04,982 --> 00:23:06,082
Let's go.

662
00:23:06,082 --> 00:23:07,352
(Dinosaur egg braised seafood from 100 million years ago)

663
00:23:07,352 --> 00:23:08,552
(An owner who doesn't fit the restaurant's theme?)

664
00:23:08,552 --> 00:23:09,782
(A dinosaur egg bowl too deep to eat from comfortably)

665
00:23:09,782 --> 00:23:11,792
We'll have to visit the last place to know.

666
00:23:11,792 --> 00:23:12,822
(Heading to the next place)

667
00:23:12,822 --> 00:23:13,922
What's that?

668
00:23:15,222 --> 00:23:16,992
- What's that? - What?

669
00:23:16,992 --> 00:23:18,392
(There's something outside the restaurant.)

670
00:23:19,392 --> 00:23:20,792
(Above the members' heads)

671
00:23:20,792 --> 00:23:22,302
- "Youth Concert?" - "Youth Concert?"

672
00:23:22,302 --> 00:23:23,402
"Youth Concert."

673
00:23:23,402 --> 00:23:24,632
(A banner advertising a concert?)

674
00:23:25,532 --> 00:23:27,232
That looks like a B-Side.

675
00:23:27,532 --> 00:23:29,142
That could be a B-Side.

676
00:23:29,672 --> 00:23:32,212
The fact that there's a "Youth Concert" banner up there...

677
00:23:32,542 --> 00:23:34,042
is so random.

678
00:23:34,372 --> 00:23:35,682
Who are the performers?

679
00:23:35,682 --> 00:23:37,442
(The banner seems oddly placed.)

680
00:23:38,012 --> 00:23:39,552
I took a photo of it.

681
00:23:40,582 --> 00:23:42,752
But it's hard to tell who the performers are.

682
00:23:43,522 --> 00:23:46,322
- Nice. -  They could be local celebrities.

683
00:23:46,322 --> 00:23:47,322
Could be.

684
00:23:47,322 --> 00:23:49,522
The guy in the poster has...

685
00:23:49,522 --> 00:23:52,262
the same hairstyle as Dae Sung during "FANTASTIC BABY."

686
00:23:52,562 --> 00:23:55,032
- His bangs are covering his eyes. - For real.

687
00:23:55,032 --> 00:23:57,032
- Right? They're covering his eyes. - Yes.

688
00:23:57,262 --> 00:23:58,372
The names are on it,

689
00:23:58,372 --> 00:23:59,472
- but I can't read them. - Right?

690
00:23:59,472 --> 00:24:00,802
I have no idea who they are.

691
00:24:01,002 --> 00:24:02,172
"With the community."

692
00:24:02,172 --> 00:24:03,502
Maybe it's HAON.

693
00:24:03,502 --> 00:24:05,942
- Who? - The name looks a lot like HAON.

694
00:24:05,942 --> 00:24:07,212
- HAON? - HAON?

695
00:24:07,212 --> 00:24:10,182
(A barely legible name?)

696
00:24:10,242 --> 00:24:11,652
It's giving HAON.

697
00:24:11,652 --> 00:24:12,652
You're right.

698
00:24:13,112 --> 00:24:15,182
"HAON" is written right here.

699
00:24:16,152 --> 00:24:18,092
(The winner of "High School Rapper 2" and "Show Me the Money 12")

700
00:24:18,392 --> 00:24:20,852
(They confirm it's HAON.)

701
00:24:20,852 --> 00:24:22,822
It says "Culinary Class Wars 2" here.

702
00:24:22,822 --> 00:24:24,262
- You're right. - I can see it now.

703
00:24:24,262 --> 00:24:26,362
- "Actress Yoon..." - Isn't it "Ga?"

704
00:24:26,362 --> 00:24:27,432
It's Yoon Ga I.

705
00:24:27,432 --> 00:24:29,532
- Yoon Ga I? - Yoon Ga I, Baby Beast, and HAON.

706
00:24:29,532 --> 00:24:31,102
Are they similar in age?

707
00:24:31,102 --> 00:24:33,102
- Yoon Ga I? - Yoon...

708
00:24:33,102 --> 00:24:35,672
(Is the connection between these three today's B-Side?)

709
00:24:36,572 --> 00:24:37,802
This time, we...

710
00:24:38,442 --> 00:24:41,312
Is it connected to that song about one million dollars?

711
00:24:41,742 --> 00:24:44,112
- The song related to money. - You could be right.

712
00:24:44,682 --> 00:24:46,212
This lineup...

713
00:24:46,212 --> 00:24:47,282
(Could this really be a B-Side?)

714
00:24:47,282 --> 00:24:49,452
- I can't see the connection. - For now, the first place...

715
00:24:49,452 --> 00:24:51,152
- is suspicious. - Totally.

716
00:24:51,152 --> 00:24:52,792
- I'm suspicious of it. - Same here.

717
00:24:53,692 --> 00:24:55,662
What was the hint for the second place?

718
00:24:56,762 --> 00:24:57,962
- Oh, right. - Wasn't it mud?

719
00:24:57,962 --> 00:24:59,462
- It was mud. - Yes, mud.

720
00:24:59,462 --> 00:25:01,062
(Second location: On-site reaction hint)

721
00:25:01,062 --> 00:25:02,862
(Oh, my. I've only used it as a face mask.)

722
00:25:02,862 --> 00:25:05,132
(We're going to eat it?)

723
00:25:05,232 --> 00:25:07,932
- Eating mud? - That's a little...

724
00:25:07,932 --> 00:25:09,302
I don't think I can.

725
00:25:09,302 --> 00:25:11,612
We'll get kidney stones.

726
00:25:12,172 --> 00:25:13,942
- For real. - That'd be bad.

727
00:25:14,142 --> 00:25:16,382
My health checkup is next week.

728
00:25:16,382 --> 00:25:17,412
Is that so?

729
00:25:17,612 --> 00:25:19,182
I can't have mud show up in my stomach.

730
00:25:20,152 --> 00:25:22,222
The doctor could be like, "Did you eat mud?"

731
00:25:22,352 --> 00:25:24,452
- "Mud?" - "Did you eat mud or something?"

732
00:25:25,622 --> 00:25:27,722
People always asked what I wanted to be when I grew up.

733
00:25:27,722 --> 00:25:28,792
I became a mud-el.

734
00:25:29,192 --> 00:25:30,862
- I'm sorry. - No, it's okay.

735
00:25:31,322 --> 00:25:33,332
(Laughing)

736
00:25:33,492 --> 00:25:36,002
That's a global joke about becoming a model.

737
00:25:36,002 --> 00:25:39,132
A mud-el joke.

738
00:25:39,132 --> 00:25:40,302
Yes, mud-el.

739
00:25:40,302 --> 00:25:43,042
I can't talk at work, so my jokes get stuck in the mud.

740
00:25:44,172 --> 00:25:45,272
Got it.

741
00:25:45,672 --> 00:25:47,112
(Nice rhyme!)

742
00:25:47,112 --> 00:25:48,382
Did you come prepared?

743
00:25:49,182 --> 00:25:50,442
(Impressed)

744
00:25:50,442 --> 00:25:51,852
- No. - She sure did.

745
00:25:52,582 --> 00:25:53,882
- Sang Yeob... - Nice.

746
00:25:53,882 --> 00:25:55,152
is jealous.

747
00:25:55,152 --> 00:25:56,152
(Laughing)

748
00:25:56,582 --> 00:25:58,122
I'm jealous of such wit, you know?

749
00:26:00,222 --> 00:26:01,922
She had her talk all planned out.

750
00:26:01,922 --> 00:26:02,922
(Even her banter is world-class.)

751
00:26:03,292 --> 00:26:04,362
We must be here.

752
00:26:04,362 --> 00:26:07,132
It's not an area where you'd expect a restaurant.

753
00:26:08,262 --> 00:26:10,032
- Craft beer? - Beer?

754
00:26:10,032 --> 00:26:12,332
The place sells beer.

755
00:26:13,802 --> 00:26:16,342
(The sign says "craft beer.")

756
00:26:16,872 --> 00:26:18,002
It must be a draft beer place.

757
00:26:18,002 --> 00:26:20,312
- Draft beer? I love draft beer. - Let's start...

758
00:26:20,312 --> 00:26:22,782
Let's start the morning with draft beer.

759
00:26:22,782 --> 00:26:24,112
(Starting the morning with draft beer)

760
00:26:24,112 --> 00:26:25,712
Let's get my morning started.

761
00:26:26,582 --> 00:26:29,152
Wait. Finding a place like this out here...

762
00:26:29,152 --> 00:26:30,782
- is surprising. - It's out of the blue.

763
00:26:30,782 --> 00:26:31,792
Right?

764
00:26:31,792 --> 00:26:33,692
The place is surrounded by rice paddies and fields.

765
00:26:33,692 --> 00:26:34,722
Exactly.

766
00:26:34,822 --> 00:26:38,092
(Beside rice paddies and fields)

767
00:26:39,632 --> 00:26:40,732
(A hip vibe)

768
00:26:40,732 --> 00:26:43,732
You have to use GPS to get here.

769
00:26:44,532 --> 00:26:46,202
This place also has a vibe.

770
00:26:46,602 --> 00:26:49,742
This place has a completely different vibe from the last one.

771
00:26:49,742 --> 00:26:51,712
(The second location has a distinctly exotic feel.)

772
00:26:51,712 --> 00:26:53,172
- It's fake. It's so fake. - Pizza?

773
00:26:53,172 --> 00:26:55,142
Everything looks a little too new.

774
00:26:55,142 --> 00:26:57,182
Nothing looks like it's been rained on. Am I right?

775
00:26:57,812 --> 00:26:59,452
- Overall. - You're right.

776
00:26:59,452 --> 00:27:00,652
(An exterior that's too clean?)

777
00:27:00,712 --> 00:27:02,282
But it would've cost a lot...

778
00:27:02,282 --> 00:27:03,852
for the production crew to decorate this place.

779
00:27:03,852 --> 00:27:05,652
- To decorate the whole place. - Yes.

780
00:27:05,722 --> 00:27:07,752
- To decorate the whole place, - To do that...

781
00:27:08,022 --> 00:27:09,722
