He must be the owner. Hello.

1298
00:45:34,498 --> 00:45:35,798
- He's wearing yellow. - Hello.

1299
00:45:35,798 --> 00:45:36,968
Hello.

1300
00:45:36,968 --> 00:45:39,138
- Hello. - He looks like Tae Jin Ah.

1301
00:45:39,138 --> 00:45:41,008
- You and this place look cool. - Hello.

1302
00:45:41,008 --> 00:45:43,978
- It's a countryside. - Hello.

1303
00:45:43,978 --> 00:45:45,108
Really?

1304
00:45:45,108 --> 00:45:46,518
- This place... - It's so pretty here.

1305
00:45:46,518 --> 00:45:49,178
Could you explain this place?

1306
00:45:49,178 --> 00:45:50,418
It's a yellow village.

1307
00:45:50,918 --> 00:45:52,318
- The village itself is? - Yes.

1308
00:45:52,318 --> 00:45:53,858
- There are ginkgo trees. - Yes.

1309
00:45:53,858 --> 00:45:56,988
In fall, they turn golden.

1310
00:45:56,988 --> 00:45:59,388
- That's why the hint said gold. - That's right.

1311
00:45:59,558 --> 00:46:02,428
It's so pretty here. Why is it one million dollars?

1312
00:46:02,798 --> 00:46:04,698
One ginkgo tree...

1313
00:46:04,698 --> 00:46:06,568
- is more than a 100 years old. - Right.

1314
00:46:06,568 --> 00:46:08,838
It's worth over 1,000 dollars.

1315
00:46:08,838 --> 00:46:10,708
And there are about 1,000 trees in this village.

1316
00:46:12,708 --> 00:46:14,838
- The total is 1 million dollars. - It'd add up to 1 million dollars.

1317
00:46:14,838 --> 00:46:15,938
You're right.

1318
00:46:16,078 --> 00:46:18,248
(It's impressive.)

1319
00:46:18,248 --> 00:46:20,548
Value-wise, it's more expensive.

1320
00:46:20,548 --> 00:46:22,048
- But that's roughly the estimate. - Yes.

1321
00:46:22,648 --> 00:46:25,788
Do you run the cafe, sir?

1322
00:46:25,788 --> 00:46:28,618
I run the hands-on farm...

1323
00:46:28,618 --> 00:46:30,258
and serve as the village head too.

1324
00:46:31,388 --> 00:46:33,858
- You're the village head? - No wonder.

1325
00:46:34,028 --> 00:46:35,428
No wonder.

1326
00:46:35,428 --> 00:46:37,698
- He looked extraordinary. - Yes.

1327
00:46:37,698 --> 00:46:39,028
- That's right. - That's right.

1328
00:46:39,028 --> 00:46:40,798
The village head usually does all the stuff.

1329
00:46:40,798 --> 00:46:41,838
That's right.

1330
00:46:43,108 --> 00:46:45,508
(Boryeong Ginkgo Village)

1331
00:46:46,068 --> 00:46:51,348
(With more than 1,000 ginkgo trees,)

1332
00:46:51,348 --> 00:46:53,618
(it glows golden in fall.)

1333
00:46:53,618 --> 00:46:57,448
I'm Kim Min Gu, the village head of the Ginkgo Village.

1334
00:46:57,918 --> 00:47:00,288
I'm the 14th generation of my family in Boryeong.

1335
00:47:00,688 --> 00:47:04,158
I was born and raised here,

1336
00:47:04,158 --> 00:47:06,928
so since I was in middle school, I helped out...

1337
00:47:06,928 --> 00:47:08,928
with the harvest of ginkgo.

1338
00:47:08,928 --> 00:47:12,128
I've been doing this job for more than 30 years.

1339
00:47:12,368 --> 00:47:14,168
To promote the village,

1340
00:47:14,168 --> 00:47:16,738
the villagers and I harvest ginkgo ourselves...

1341
00:47:16,738 --> 00:47:20,308
and have developed this, which you can taste only in here.

1342
00:47:20,438 --> 00:47:22,808
I thought if I could create a fairy tale-like village,

1343
00:47:22,808 --> 00:47:27,148
people would want to visit and live here.

1344
00:47:28,348 --> 00:47:31,788
So we decorated the cups, curtains, and everything...

1345
00:47:31,788 --> 00:47:33,118
in yellow.

1346
00:47:33,118 --> 00:47:34,218
(Everything including the ginkgo leaves is yellow.)

1347
00:47:34,218 --> 00:47:36,928
The village is full of things to see and enjoy.

1348
00:47:37,028 --> 00:47:40,358
During the ginkgo season, thousands of people visit per day.

1349
00:47:40,358 --> 00:47:42,898
(During the ginkgo season, 2,000 people visit per day.)

1350
00:47:43,128 --> 00:47:45,968
The owner is obsessed with ginkgo.

1351
00:47:45,968 --> 00:47:47,438
Everything here is yellow.

1352
00:47:47,998 --> 00:47:51,108
Sixth Sense crew, is this place real?

1353
00:47:52,208 --> 00:47:54,778
It's so pretty.

1354
00:47:55,778 --> 00:47:58,308
- Fall is coming. - Yes.

1355
00:47:58,308 --> 00:48:01,118
From the end of October to mid-November.

1356
00:48:01,118 --> 00:48:02,378
- It's lovely. - That's the season.

1357
00:48:02,378 --> 00:48:03,718
(The ginkgo trees are the prettiest from October to November.)

1358
00:48:03,718 --> 00:48:06,318
- The fields turn golden too. - That's right.

1359
00:48:06,318 --> 00:48:07,858
I can imagine how pretty it'll be.

1360
00:48:07,858 --> 00:48:09,588
(From the trees to the fields, the whole village turns golden.)

1361
00:48:09,588 --> 00:48:11,488
- You should come now. - Now.

1362
00:48:11,488 --> 00:48:12,588
Now's the season.

1363
00:48:12,588 --> 00:48:15,028
(It's a perfect spot for a late fall trip.)

1364
00:48:15,258 --> 00:48:17,398
- Since we're here... - Yes.

1365
00:48:17,398 --> 00:48:19,228
Is that ginkgo bread?

1366
00:48:19,228 --> 00:48:20,768
- Yes. - What's that?

1367
00:48:21,438 --> 00:48:24,808
(There's bread made of ginkgo?)

1368
00:48:24,808 --> 00:48:28,108
- The trend nowadays is about bread. - Yes.

1369
00:48:28,108 --> 00:48:29,948
Since three years ago, we wanted to promote the village...

1370
00:48:29,948 --> 00:48:31,778
with ginkgo bread.

1371
00:48:31,778 --> 00:48:34,918
- Really? - We've developed it.

1372
00:48:34,918 --> 00:48:36,648
You can experience it...

1373
00:48:36,648 --> 00:48:37,918
and taste it too.

1374
00:48:37,918 --> 00:48:39,448
(Everyone seems to be unfamiliar with it.)

1375
00:48:39,448 --> 00:48:41,988
- Could we have a look at it? - Sure.

1376
00:48:41,988 --> 00:48:43,228
- Shall we go? - Okay.

1377
00:48:43,358 --> 00:48:45,758
- Can we go inside and see? - Yes, you can.

1378
00:48:45,758 --> 00:48:46,928
(Looking forward to it)

1379
00:48:47,698 --> 00:48:49,158
There are so many pretty places.

1380
00:48:49,158 --> 00:48:50,228
(Let's go try the ginkgo bread.)

1381
00:48:51,168 --> 00:48:52,468
I love it.

1382
00:48:52,698 --> 00:48:54,638
- I want to live here. - Me too.

1383
00:48:55,068 --> 00:48:57,208
- It's already... - This...

1384
00:48:57,708 --> 00:48:59,368
It's cute.

1385
00:49:00,838 --> 00:49:02,008
It smells savory.

1386
00:49:02,008 --> 00:49:03,078
(There's savory smell in the yellow container.)

1387
00:49:03,078 --> 00:49:04,448
It's ginkgo bread.

1388
00:49:04,578 --> 00:49:06,048
(Are you here for the ginkgo bread?)

1389
00:49:06,048 --> 00:49:08,518
- This is automated. - Yes, this...

1390
00:49:08,518 --> 00:49:10,348
- It's cute. - This is...

1391
00:49:10,488 --> 00:49:12,118
It has ginkgo leaves.

1392
00:49:12,118 --> 00:49:13,258
It has ginkgo leaves in it?

1393
00:49:13,258 --> 00:49:14,258
- Yes. Look here. - My goodness.

1394
00:49:14,258 --> 00:49:15,758
And there's a ginkgo nut inside.

1395
00:49:15,758 --> 00:49:16,788
- Really? - It has a ginkgo nut in it.

1396
00:49:16,788 --> 00:49:17,928
There's a ginkgo nut inside.

1397
00:49:17,928 --> 00:49:19,958
- It has a ginkgo nut inside. - There's a ginkgo nut inside.

1398
00:49:20,228 --> 00:49:22,958
Since ginkgo nuts are Ginkgo Village's local specialty,

1399
00:49:22,958 --> 00:49:25,468
we decided to develop and make a ginkgo cake.

1400
00:49:25,468 --> 00:49:26,898
That's how we came up with it.

1401
00:49:27,338 --> 00:49:29,908
It's made with ginkgo powder and Korean wheat.

1402
00:49:30,368 --> 00:49:33,108
Plus, we fill it with sweet potato paste.

1403
00:49:34,838 --> 00:49:37,708
We tried putting candied ginkgo nuts in it,

1404
00:49:37,708 --> 00:49:39,878
and it turned out so chewy and delicious.

1405
00:49:40,448 --> 00:49:42,148
People say it's cute, pretty,

1406
00:49:42,148 --> 00:49:45,618
and has a rich, nutty flavor.

1407
00:49:45,748 --> 00:49:48,058
(It's available only here.)

1408
00:49:48,658 --> 00:49:51,058
It's just like how Cheonan is famous for walnut cakes.

1409
00:49:52,028 --> 00:49:54,298
- There's no way this could be fake. - Let's try it.

1410
00:49:54,558 --> 00:49:56,428
- It smells so nutty and savory. - It smells nutty.

1411
00:49:56,428 --> 00:49:58,268
- There's a ginkgo nut inside. - It has one piece each.

1412
00:49:58,268 --> 00:49:59,698
- There's a ginkgo nut inside. - Here.

1413
00:49:59,698 --> 00:50:00,698
Would you like to try it?

1414
00:50:00,698 --> 00:50:01,738
- Let's try it. - Okay.

1415
00:50:01,738 --> 00:50:02,868
It's still hot.

1416
00:50:02,868 --> 00:50:04,768
- Hold it with both hands. - Okay.

1417
00:50:04,768 --> 00:50:06,138
- It's hot. - Gosh, it's hot!

1418
00:50:06,138 --> 00:50:07,138
(Juggling it with both hands)

1419
00:50:07,438 --> 00:50:09,778
- Here. - It's really hot.

1420
00:50:10,478 --> 00:50:11,708
It's really hot.

1421
00:50:11,778 --> 00:50:13,118
- Hang on. It's hot. - My goodness.

1422
00:50:13,118 --> 00:50:14,278
- It's hot. - It'll cool down in no time.

1423
00:50:14,278 --> 00:50:15,348
(Rolling it for a while)

1424
00:50:15,348 --> 00:50:17,488
- I can't touch something hot. - Really?

1425
00:50:17,488 --> 00:50:19,018
- This is a cold one. - I'll have a cold one too.

1426
00:50:19,518 --> 00:50:21,818
- No. - It's too hot.

1427
00:50:22,118 --> 00:50:23,528
- But it tastes good. - This is okay.

1428
00:50:24,588 --> 00:50:25,988
(A taste that calls for applause)

1429
00:50:25,988 --> 00:50:27,028
It's so good.

1430
00:50:27,558 --> 00:50:29,328
There's a subtle hint of ginkgo aroma,

1431
00:50:29,328 --> 00:50:31,668
and it pairs so well with the sweet potato.

1432
00:50:31,668 --> 00:50:32,928
(The sweet potato paste harmonizes with the ginkgo aroma.)

1433
00:50:33,598 --> 00:50:36,538
(Exclaiming)

1434
00:50:36,738 --> 00:50:37,838
- But it tastes good. - This is okay.

1435
00:50:37,968 --> 00:50:39,538
- It's so good. - It's not too hot.

1436
00:50:40,078 --> 00:50:41,478
- It's really good. - Look here.

1437
00:50:41,738 --> 00:50:43,348
- They also have a ginkgo latte. - Ginkgo latte!

1438
00:50:43,348 --> 00:50:44,378
Yes.

1439
00:50:44,948 --> 00:50:46,848
(Another signature menu item of Ginkgo Village)

1440
00:50:47,318 --> 00:50:48,448
- Smoothie. - Ginkgo smoothie...

1441
00:50:48,448 --> 00:50:49,818
- and ginkgo vinegar ade. - Vinegar ade.

1442
00:50:49,818 --> 00:50:51,188
(Ginkgo drink trio)

1443
00:50:51,548 --> 00:50:53,258
I should try the ginkgo latte.

1444
00:50:53,418 --> 00:50:54,518
- I'll have a ginkgo vinegar ade. - Me too.

1445
00:50:54,518 --> 00:50:55,618
- Ginkgo vinegar ade. - I'll have the ade.

1446
00:50:55,618 --> 00:50:57,158
- I'll have a ginkgo vinegar ade. - I'll have a smoothie.

1447
00:50:57,458 --> 00:50:58,628
- Smoothie? - Okay.

1448
00:50:58,758 --> 00:51:00,798
I'll get the drinks ready and bring them right over to you.

1449
00:51:00,998 --> 00:51:02,798
- I downed it in a single bite. - It tastes good.

1450
00:51:02,798 --> 00:51:04,228
(They head to their seats enjoying the ginkgo cakes.)

1451
00:51:04,398 --> 00:51:05,528
It's good even when it's cold.

1452
00:51:05,528 --> 00:51:08,168
Wait, they have something like this even here.

1453
00:51:08,568 --> 00:51:10,368
(Sang Yeob spots something?)

1454
00:51:10,368 --> 00:51:12,038
- There's a radio here too. - Right.

1455
00:51:13,738 --> 00:51:15,508
Why is a radio here?

1456
00:51:16,378 --> 00:51:18,508
(A suspiciously placed radio)

1457
00:51:18,508 --> 00:51:20,218
This could be a B-Side clue.

1458
00:51:21,548 --> 00:51:23,918
Does it have something to do with a radio this time?

1459
00:51:23,918 --> 00:51:24,948
What could it be?

1460
00:51:25,948 --> 00:51:27,158
What do the clues mean?

1461
00:51:27,158 --> 00:51:28,588
"SUN" and "RADIO."

1462
00:51:29,658 --> 00:51:33,328
There was also a radio at the first place.

1463
00:51:33,458 --> 00:51:36,258
- Was there a radio? - There were some old radios.

1464
00:51:36,768 --> 00:51:38,728
- Sun. - The sun is red.

1465
00:51:38,998 --> 00:51:40,698
And the dinosaur egg braised seafood was red earlier.

1466
00:51:41,338 --> 00:51:42,738
It can't be that simple, right?

1467
00:51:43,408 --> 00:51:44,508
No.

1468
00:51:44,938 --> 00:51:46,778
- Hyun Ji. - I'm losing confidence...

1469
00:51:46,778 --> 00:51:48,308
since you glare at me like that.

1470
00:51:49,908 --> 00:51:52,208
Why are you intimidating me?

1471
00:51:53,378 --> 00:51:54,878
You're not Yoon Ju, right?

1472
00:51:55,478 --> 00:51:56,488
She looks like Yoon Ju.

1473
00:51:56,488 --> 00:51:58,218
- She's like Yoon Ju. - Even the way she talks.

1474
00:51:58,218 --> 00:51:59,688
- Hyun Ji and Yoon Ju look alike. - Hyun Ji sounds...

1475
00:51:59,688 --> 00:52:01,518
just like Yoon Ju.

1476
00:52:02,018 --> 00:52:03,588
I'm the much more westernized...

1477
00:52:03,588 --> 00:52:06,498
and evolved version.

1478
00:52:07,228 --> 00:52:08,728
- Evolved? - You sound like her even now.

1479
00:52:08,728 --> 00:52:10,268
Even acting like this reminds us of her.

1480
00:52:10,798 --> 00:52:14,298
Yoon Ju told me that I looked really westernized.

1481
00:52:15,038 --> 00:52:17,138
- Really? - We have a league of our own.

1482
00:52:17,138 --> 00:52:18,168
You do?

1483
00:52:19,138 --> 00:52:21,508
(The most Western-looking among Eastern-looking faces)

1484
00:52:21,508 --> 00:52:23,948
Don't you think this place is real? I think it's real.

1485
00:52:23,948 --> 00:52:26,408
- I don't suspect this place at all. - This is...

1486
00:52:26,778 --> 00:52:28,448
But they could've painted...

1487
00:52:28,448 --> 00:52:30,618
this place yellow at the last minute.

1488
00:52:30,918 --> 00:52:32,448
They look quite new, right?

1489
00:52:32,448 --> 00:52:34,358
Everything here looks new.

1490
00:52:34,618 --> 00:52:36,018
Actually, if they wanted to stage all this,

1491
00:52:36,018 --> 00:52:37,388
- they could. - Definitely.

1492
00:52:37,588 --> 00:52:40,158
Still, this isn't the kind of scale just 1 or 2 people could pull off.

1493
00:52:40,158 --> 00:52:41,858
- If it were fake. - Right.

1494
00:52:41,998 --> 00:52:43,298
Look. Everything is yellow.

1495
00:52:43,298 --> 00:52:45,068
(Painting the whole village yellow?)

1496
00:52:45,068 --> 00:52:47,338
(It's way too big a scale for the production crew to stage.)

1497
00:52:47,638 --> 00:52:50,338
By the way, what did you think of the village head?

1498
00:52:51,008 --> 00:52:52,868
- He did seem like a village head. - He seemed real.

1499
00:52:52,868 --> 00:52:53,938
He seemed real.

1500
00:52:53,938 --> 00:52:55,008
- That's how you felt? - Yes.

1501
00:52:55,008 --> 00:52:57,178
- Did you think he seemed fake? - I thought he was an actor.

1502
00:52:57,178 --> 00:52:58,248
- Really? - Yes.

1503
00:52:58,248 --> 00:52:59,248
Didn't he look like an actor?

1504
00:52:59,248 --> 00:53:00,348
- He looked like an actor, right? - Yes.

1505
00:53:00,448 --> 00:53:02,048
I think the village head is real.

1506
00:53:02,048 --> 00:53:03,818
I bet he's an ambassador for this place.

1507
00:53:04,088 --> 00:53:05,388
(A sharp insight from a C ambassador)

1508
00:53:05,388 --> 00:53:08,558
- An ambassador for this place? - She's an expert on that stuff.

1509
00:53:08,558 --> 00:53:09,718
She knows stuff like that well.

1510
00:53:09,718 --> 00:53:10,928
That makes sense.

1511
00:53:10,928 --> 00:53:12,028
(That sounds somewhat plausible.)

1512
00:53:12,028 --> 00:53:13,298
- The ambassador for ginkgo trees. - Right.

1513
00:53:13,298 --> 00:53:15,028
- He's an ambassador? - Ambassador.

1514
00:53:15,028 --> 00:53:16,398
(Is he a real village head who's the village's ambassador?)

1515
00:53:16,698 --> 00:53:19,298
(Ta-da)

1516
00:53:20,338 --> 00:53:22,138
(Ta-da?)

1517
00:53:22,438 --> 00:53:23,738
- "Ta-da?" - "Ta-da?"

1518
00:53:23,908 --> 00:53:25,068
That sounds really awkward.

1519
00:53:25,068 --> 00:53:26,068
- Hang on. - This will be delicious.

1520
00:53:26,068 --> 00:53:27,808
Did you become village head by a vote?

1521
00:53:28,308 --> 00:53:29,378
- Me? - Yes.

1522
00:53:29,638 --> 00:53:30,878
I was the only nominee.

1523
00:53:31,208 --> 00:53:32,778
No one volunteered.

1524
00:53:33,108 --> 00:53:34,748
- Did you run unopposed? - I was the only one.

1525
00:53:35,178 --> 00:53:36,218
I see.

1526
00:53:36,888 --> 00:53:37,948
Okay.

1527
00:53:38,288 --> 00:53:39,518
- Please enjoy your food. - Thank you.

1528
00:53:39,518 --> 00:53:41,458
- Thank you. - Thank you for the food.

1529
00:53:41,458 --> 00:53:42,518
- This is... - He sounded...

1530
00:53:42,518 --> 00:53:44,188
- quite awkward. - "Ta-da."

1531
00:53:44,428 --> 00:53:46,088
- Why did he suddenly say that? - I know. It was awkward.

1532
00:53:46,088 --> 00:53:48,028
He had a bit of a crazy look in his eyes.

1533
00:53:48,028 --> 00:53:49,658
- Isn't he an actor? - I was surprised.

1534
00:53:50,068 --> 00:53:51,068
(An extraordinary glint in his eyes)

1535
00:53:51,068 --> 00:53:52,468
I was startled.

1536
00:53:52,768 --> 00:53:54,238
(Acting with her eyes)

1537
00:53:54,238 --> 00:53:55,298
My goodness.

1538
00:53:55,798 --> 00:53:57,408
(Taking a sip of Sang Yeob's ginkgo vinegar ade)

1539
00:53:58,808 --> 00:53:59,808
(Shouting)

1540
00:54:00,138 --> 00:54:01,238
Why? Is it sour?

1541
00:54:01,578 --> 00:54:02,808
It's real vinegar.

1542
00:54:02,808 --> 00:54:05,208
(It's real vinegar.)

1543
00:54:05,748 --> 00:54:07,348
(Let me try.)

1544
00:54:07,548 --> 00:54:08,778
Would you like to try this?

1545
00:54:09,118 --> 00:54:10,418
- Why? - This is...

