I am Heo Jin Gyu, Ulsan Metropolitan City...

1797
01:03:00,885 --> 01:03:02,585
Intangible Cultural Heritage Number Four Onggi Master.

1798
01:03:02,885 --> 01:03:04,515
- He's a master. - A master?

1799
01:03:04,515 --> 01:03:06,185
Isn't this way too high-quality just to trick us?!

1800
01:03:06,185 --> 01:03:07,685
- Onggi Master. - You went to a master craftsman...

1801
01:03:07,685 --> 01:03:09,185
just to deceive us?

1802
01:03:09,255 --> 01:03:10,725
Isn't that a work of art?

1803
01:03:11,695 --> 01:03:13,965
I need to prep the clay right away.

1804
01:03:14,525 --> 01:03:15,525
Today...

1805
01:03:15,525 --> 01:03:17,535
After shaping this onggi,

1806
01:03:17,535 --> 01:03:19,695
it needs to dry for about 15 days,

1807
01:03:19,695 --> 01:03:21,505
get glazed, and cure...

1808
01:03:21,505 --> 01:03:25,235
for another 15 days before going into the kiln.

1809
01:03:25,375 --> 01:03:28,405
So it needs about a month to complete the process.

1810
01:03:28,945 --> 01:03:31,045
That's the only way it can withstand the heat.

1811
01:03:31,045 --> 01:03:34,285
I have to go without sleep, constantly going back and forth...

1812
01:03:34,515 --> 01:03:37,155
to tend to the pieces according to their drying schedule.

1813
01:03:37,155 --> 01:03:38,315
Seriously?

1814
01:03:38,615 --> 01:03:40,355
Aren't you putting a master through too much trouble...

1815
01:03:40,355 --> 01:03:42,685
- just to trick us? - I know.

1816
01:03:42,855 --> 01:03:44,425
- True. - Just to fool the few of us.

1817
01:03:44,955 --> 01:03:46,055
Who's that?

1818
01:03:46,825 --> 01:03:47,925
A braised seafood master?

1819
01:03:49,095 --> 01:03:51,835
(The flavor that washed away...)

1820
01:03:51,835 --> 01:03:55,265
(the Sixth Sense members' doubts)

1821
01:03:55,565 --> 01:03:58,235
I've been running a braised monkfish restaurant...

1822
01:03:58,235 --> 01:04:00,205
- in this spot for nearly 30 years. - Seoul's top 3 famous spots?

1823
01:04:00,205 --> 01:04:01,705
My name is No Jae Gyeong.

1824
01:04:02,105 --> 01:04:04,945
We heard this place is famous for braised seafood.

1825
01:04:04,945 --> 01:04:07,485
Could we possibly get some of your secret sauce?

1826
01:04:08,345 --> 01:04:09,445
All right.

1827
01:04:10,585 --> 01:04:11,915
It was just too good!

1828
01:04:12,615 --> 01:04:13,925
It was too delicious!

1829
01:04:15,155 --> 01:04:17,495
Yaksu-dong!

1830
01:04:17,725 --> 01:04:21,125
- The flavor was clean and spot-on. - It's so close.

1831
01:04:21,695 --> 01:04:23,895
- No wonder it was so tasty. - It was so good.

1832
01:04:23,895 --> 01:04:25,995
- True. It was so good. - We couldn't doubt...

1833
01:04:25,995 --> 01:04:28,105
- about the taste. - Right.

1834
01:04:28,835 --> 01:04:31,235
Putting such precious people through all this trouble just to fool me...

1835
01:04:31,775 --> 01:04:34,545
- Today's round is such a bummer. - Right.

1836
01:04:34,675 --> 01:04:36,105
Sixth Sense members,

1837
01:04:36,105 --> 01:04:38,675
- this place is fake! - We could've gotten it right.

1838
01:04:38,675 --> 01:04:40,145
I'm about to pass out.

1839
01:04:40,145 --> 01:04:41,945
I should've won at rock-paper-scissors.

1840
01:04:41,945 --> 01:04:43,585
(And for the fake dinosaur egg...)

1841
01:04:44,855 --> 01:04:46,485
- B-Side! - B-Side.

1842
01:04:46,955 --> 01:04:50,995
(Did you try not to miss any passing B-Side clues today?)

1843
01:04:51,555 --> 01:04:53,455
Where were they? What was it?

1844
01:04:53,655 --> 01:04:54,765
Let's see.

1845
01:04:55,725 --> 01:04:57,365
(Since you'd been finding the B-Sides way too easily lately,)

1846
01:04:57,365 --> 01:04:59,365
(we decided to raise the difficulty.)

1847
01:04:59,365 --> 01:05:01,205
The production crew lately...

1848
01:05:01,205 --> 01:05:03,535
(You would've missed it if you had only looked straight ahead.)

1849
01:05:03,535 --> 01:05:04,775
(Today's B-Side)

1850
01:05:04,775 --> 01:05:05,875
What is it?

1851
01:05:05,875 --> 01:05:06,975
(Up and Down)

1852
01:05:06,975 --> 01:05:08,245
- What? - What is it?

1853
01:05:08,545 --> 01:05:10,505
(What does that mean?)

1854
01:05:10,715 --> 01:05:12,545
We did see the drones, though.

1855
01:05:12,545 --> 01:05:14,315
- What was down there? - Down?

1856
01:05:14,315 --> 01:05:15,445
What was there?

1857
01:05:15,985 --> 01:05:17,415
(First)

1858
01:05:17,415 --> 01:05:18,915
(This plaza you walked across)

1859
01:05:18,915 --> 01:05:20,685
- Right. - What was at the plaza?

1860
01:05:21,055 --> 01:05:22,255
(Was it up above?)

1861
01:05:22,255 --> 01:05:23,255
Up.

1862
01:05:24,125 --> 01:05:25,195
Down.

1863
01:05:25,325 --> 01:05:26,795
(The answer is...)

1864
01:05:26,795 --> 01:05:27,865
The answer?

1865
01:05:27,865 --> 01:05:29,395
(Down!)

1866
01:05:29,725 --> 01:05:31,335
(If you'd looked down at the plaza floor...)

1867
01:05:31,335 --> 01:05:32,435
What was there?

1868
01:05:33,235 --> 01:05:35,565
- Was there anything like that? - Is it water?

1869
01:05:36,105 --> 01:05:37,305
What?

1870
01:05:37,305 --> 01:05:38,875
It's a drawing.

1871
01:05:39,075 --> 01:05:40,275
What do you see?

1872
01:05:40,745 --> 01:05:41,805
What is this?

1873
01:05:42,675 --> 01:05:43,675
(Let's pull back a little further.)

1874
01:05:43,675 --> 01:05:45,575
- Is it a dinosaur egg? - Dinosaur?

1875
01:05:45,575 --> 01:05:46,975
I don't think it's a dinosaur egg.

1876
01:05:47,145 --> 01:05:48,845
Gosh, what is this?

1877
01:05:50,415 --> 01:05:51,685
- It's Dooly. - Dooly.

1878
01:05:51,685 --> 01:05:52,755
Dooly?

1879
01:05:53,315 --> 01:05:55,225
(Dooly)

1880
01:05:55,225 --> 01:05:57,425
- It's unbelievable. - It's incredible.

1881
01:05:57,825 --> 01:05:59,095
Did a master painter come out here?

1882
01:05:59,095 --> 01:06:01,195
- Seriously? - Why are you doing all this?

1883
01:06:01,195 --> 01:06:03,765
Why waste such high-end talent on this?

1884
01:06:03,895 --> 01:06:05,465
(Huge Dooly)

1885
01:06:05,465 --> 01:06:06,635
I had no idea.

1886
01:06:06,635 --> 01:06:08,265
They could've drawn it a little smaller.

1887
01:06:08,265 --> 01:06:09,565
(It was right under your feet.)

1888
01:06:09,935 --> 01:06:12,035
(The next B-Side is up above.)

1889
01:06:12,035 --> 01:06:13,405
- The drones. - The drones.

1890
01:06:13,405 --> 01:06:14,805
The drones?

1891
01:06:14,905 --> 01:06:17,075
- What about it? - What was this?

1892
01:06:17,615 --> 01:06:19,375
We saw it, but we just couldn't crack it.

1893
01:06:19,745 --> 01:06:20,815
Who are they?

1894
01:06:21,085 --> 01:06:22,115
(You figured out who those three people were, right?)

1895
01:06:22,115 --> 01:06:24,555
- Baby Beast and Ga I. - Baby Beast.

1896
01:06:24,555 --> 01:06:26,685
- HAON. - What do they all have in common?

1897
01:06:27,155 --> 01:06:28,955
What is it?

1898
01:06:28,955 --> 01:06:30,655
(We were all born in 2000, the Year of the Dragon.)

1899
01:06:30,655 --> 01:06:31,955
I knew it.

1900
01:06:31,955 --> 01:06:34,595
(And if you abbreviate "2000-born Dragon?")

1901
01:06:34,595 --> 01:06:35,965
(The word 0-Dragon sounds like a dinosaur in Korean.)

1902
01:06:37,125 --> 01:06:39,535
- Dinosaur. - Come on! Zero dragon?

1903
01:06:39,635 --> 01:06:40,965
I can't believe this.

1904
01:06:41,035 --> 01:06:42,405
Then what's up with "SUN" and "RADIO?"

1905
01:06:42,405 --> 01:06:43,665
- Right. Sun and radio. - Sun.

1906
01:06:43,935 --> 01:06:47,905
(Two yellow kites flying above Ginkgo Village)

1907
01:06:48,475 --> 01:06:51,145
- Radio and sun. - Right. This is it.

1908
01:06:51,145 --> 01:06:52,345
What were the kites for?

1909
01:06:52,675 --> 01:06:54,515
- Why is it a dinosaur? - Why dinosaur?

1910
01:06:55,045 --> 01:06:56,345
Radio and sun.

1911
01:06:57,485 --> 01:06:59,685
(The way to turn these into "dinosaur" is...)

1912
01:06:59,685 --> 01:07:01,255
(by rearranging the letters.)

1913
01:07:01,255 --> 01:07:02,585
That's it?

1914
01:07:02,585 --> 01:07:04,155
- Really? - An anagram?

1915
01:07:04,895 --> 01:07:06,925
(Let's break down the words.)

1916
01:07:09,925 --> 01:07:11,395
(Rearranging the letters spells out...)

1917
01:07:12,165 --> 01:07:13,335
(Dinosaur)

1918
01:07:13,335 --> 01:07:14,965
- Dinosaur? - Dinosaur!

1919
01:07:15,735 --> 01:07:16,735
(Screaming)

1920
01:07:17,705 --> 01:07:18,735
(I can't believe we missed that.)

1921
01:07:18,735 --> 01:07:20,205
- Dinosaur. - This is really...

1922
01:07:20,905 --> 01:07:23,445
They gave us way too much credit.

1923
01:07:23,775 --> 01:07:26,775
I did suspect the first place.

1924
01:07:27,045 --> 01:07:29,415
But we misread the clues.

1925
01:07:29,415 --> 01:07:31,155
Right. We did see the clues.

1926
01:07:31,155 --> 01:07:33,085
Watching the show on TV,

1927
01:07:33,385 --> 01:07:35,155
I thought it looked super easy.

1928
01:07:35,325 --> 01:07:39,025
But being here in person, I realized it was a battle of wits.

1929
01:07:40,595 --> 01:07:42,965
We'd like to thank everyone who joined us today.

1930
01:07:42,965 --> 01:07:44,965
- Thank you. - Boryeong is beautiful.

1931
01:07:44,965 --> 01:07:45,965
(Please visit the beautiful places of Boryeong.)

1932
01:07:46,035 --> 01:07:50,465
(Season Finale in Jeju)

1933
01:07:50,535 --> 01:07:53,335
(Current Score: Production Crew 4, Sixth Sense Crew 5)

1934
01:07:53,375 --> 01:07:55,145
(The highly anticipated final guests)

1935
